course: dictionary
lesson: 2084
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must read the sentence to find the right one. «Consultation» can mean a meeting with an expert, asking people for their views, or looking something up. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: «The council ran a public consultation before building the new playground.» The clues are public, before and building. Here consultation means asking ordinary people what they think before a decision is made.
explain: When a doctor or lawyer gives advice, that is a consultation too. «She had a free consultation with the lawyer» means she got advice from an expert, and it cost nothing. Ask yourself who is meeting, and why. The answer points to the right meaning.
fact: Consultation means a meeting with an expert, such as a doctor or lawyer, to get advice.
fact: Consultation can also mean asking people for their views before making a decision.
fact: «In consultation with» means together with others, after asking for their opinions: «after consultation with parents».
fact: «Public consultation» means ordinary people are asked what they think about a plan, such as a new playground.
fact: In a formal sense, consultation means looking something up in a book or source, as in «consultation of the map».
exercise: «The school changed the uniform after consultation with parents.» What does consultation mean here? | *Asking people for their views before deciding | Looking up a word in a dictionary | A loud argument in the hall | A meeting with a doctor for health advice
exercise: «She had a free consultation with the lawyer about her will.» What is the consultation here? | *A meeting with an expert to get advice | A party to celebrate a birthday | A long holiday by the sea | A test at school
exercise: «The council ran a public consultation on the new park.» What does this tell you? | *People were asked what they thought before the decision | The council forgot about the plan | The park was already finished | Nobody was allowed to visit the park
test: In the phrase «consultation of the map», what does consultation mean? | Losing the map | *Looking something up on a map | Folding the map away | Painting the map
test: Which sentence shows a consultation with an expert? | *Dad took Gran to see the doctor for advice | The class voted on a name for the hamster | Mum asked the class for their favourite colour | The team drew a picture together
exam: Why is it helpful to read the words around consultation? | Words around it are never useful | It makes the sentence longer | *They show which meaning fits, because the clues point to it | Only the first word of a sentence matters
